NNAAMMEE
       tzselect - select a timezone

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       ttzzsseelleecctt [ --cc _c_o_o_r_d ] [ --nn _l_i_m_i_t ] [ ----hheellpp ] [ ----vveerrssiioonn ]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       The  ttzzsseelleecctt  program  asks the user for information about the current
       location, and outputs the resulting timezone to standard  output.   The
       output is suitable as a value for the TZ environment variable.

       All  interaction  with the user is done via standard input and standard
       error.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       --cc _c_o_o_r_d
              Instead of asking for continent and then country and then  city,
              ask for selection from time zones whose largest cities are clos‐
              est  to  the  location with geographical coordinates _c_o_o_r_d_.  Use
              ISO 6709 notation for _c_o_o_r_d_, that  is,  a  latitude  immediately
              followed  by  a longitude.  The latitude and longitude should be
              signed integers followed by an optional decimal point and  frac‐
              tion:  positive numbers represent north and east, negative south
              and west.  Latitudes with two and longitudes with three  integer
              digits  are  treated  as degrees; latitudes with four or six and
              longitudes with five or seven  integer  digits  are  treated  as
              _D_D_M_M_,  _D_D_D_M_M_, _D_D_M_M_S_S_, or _D_D_D_M_M_S_S representing _D_D or _D_D_D degrees,
              _M_M minutes, and zero or _S_S seconds, with any trailing  fractions
              represent fractional minutes or (if _S_S is present) seconds.  The
              decimal  point  is  that of the current locale.  For example, in
              the (default) C locale, --cc ++4400..668899--007744..004455 specifies 40.689  de‐
              grees  N,  74.045 degrees W, --cc ++44004411..44--0077440022..77 specifies 40 de‐
              grees  41.4  minutes  N,  74  degrees   2.7   minutes   W,   and
              --cc ++440044112211--00774400224400 specifies 40 degrees 41 minutes 21 seconds N,
              74  degrees  2 minutes 40 seconds W.  If _c_o_o_r_d is not one of the
              documented forms, the resulting behavior is unspecified.

       --nn _l_i_m_i_t
              When --cc is used, display the closest  _l_i_m_i_t  locations  (default
              10).

       ----hheellpp Output help information and exit.

